-   "instructions": "# App Store Public Reads (MCP)\n\nRead-only, normalized public-data reads of App Store applications exposed through the ReplyNodes App Store public-read service: app lookup, bounded term search, and related-app listings.\n\n## Surface status\n-The three documented read operations have stable public contracts with bounded requests and normalized v1 responses.\n-Route paths in this catalog are stable capability identifiers used for agent tool bindings; public gateway exposure for this platform is issued to your workspace at onboarding and must not be assumed reachable anywhere else.\n\n## How to call\n- Use the fixed gateway URL: https://api.replynodes.com\n- Each tool maps to one HTTP GET capability: substitute path parameters into the endpoint path and pass optional parameters as query strings.\n- Authenticate at the gateway with header 'Authorization: Bearer ***' or follow x402 v2 payment requirements returned as HTTP 402; the manifest holds no key or payer material.\n\n## Results\n- Success: '{\"data\": [app records], \"meta\": {\"request_id\": \"req-...\", \"contract_version\": \"v1\", \"generated_at\": \"...\", \"availability\": \"complete\"}}'.\n- Failure: '{\"error\": {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"request_id\": \"req-...\"}}'. honor HTTP status and any 'Retry-After' on 429.\n\n## Conduct\n- Read-only: these tools never mutate anything; refuse requests asking them to purchase, review, submit, or touch accounts.\n",
